WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.710
- [Narrator] Donald Trump's alleged role

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.690
in paying hush money to a porn star

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.580
could soon lead to criminal charges

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.240
against the former president,
a first in US history.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.400
Exclusive articles The Wall
Street Journal published

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.610
in 2018 triggered this
investigation into Trump.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.890
And reporter Joe Palazzolo
is still digging.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.380
- I did not expect five years later

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.810
to be still talking
about this case at all.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:22.710
- [Narrator] As a grand jury

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.540
is concluding its investigation,

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.660
let's look at the reporting
that led to this pivotal moment

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.313
and what could come next.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.650
Let's start in 2016, days
before Trump's election victory.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.050
- [Crowd] U-S-A, U-S-A.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.480
- [Narrator] And years before
porn star Stormy Daniels

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.610
would tell her side in Prime Time.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:42.690
- And you had sex with him?

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.523
- Yes.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.560
- You were 27, he was 60.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.240
Were you physically attracted to him?

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.140
- No.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.520
- Not at all.
- No.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.170
- [Narrator] During the 2016 campaign,

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.450
Daniels and her manager
were shopping her story

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.090
of an alleged affair with
Trump from a decade earlier.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.970
- She'd been onto successful
celebrity magazines

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.830
and the tabloids didn't wanna buy it.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.780
- [Narrator] Michael Cohen,
Trump's personal lawyer

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.490
at the time, was also approached

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.710
with an offer to buy Daniels' story.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.090
That was in September.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.480
- Cohen says, go to hell, essentially, no.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.190
And then Access Hollywood happens.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.930
- [Trump] And when you're
a star, they let you do it.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.040
You can do anything.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:17.873
- [Billy Bush] Whatever you want.

00:01:17.873 --> 00:01:18.870
- [Trump] Grab 'em by the (beep).

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.370
- And then boom, it's like a 180.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.710
Stormy's lawyer is back
on the phone with Cohen

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.450
and they're hashing out a deal.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.660
- [Narrator] Daniels agrees
to $130,000 for her story

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.460
in exchange for her silence,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.760
and signs a contract
on October 28th, 2016.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.790
Journal reporters caught wind
of Daniels around this time

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.160
and over months worked to piece the story

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.840
of the payment together.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.557
- So the first story ran in January, 2018,

00:01:42.557 --> 00:01:44.130
and it was pretty bare bones.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.270
I mean, what we said is what we knew

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.240
which is that Michael Cohen
had arranged $130,000 payment

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.500
to Stormy Daniels.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.490
And so we had confirmed

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.950
that he'd used a Delaware
Limited Liability Company,

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.810
a shell company essentially,
to transfer the payment.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.660
And so those were the two
stories that we reported in 2018

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.100
that really got the ball rolling.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.380
- [Narrator] A political
firestorm erupted.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.710
Trump denied the affair and
knowledge of the payment.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.100
- Well, you'll have to ask Michael Cohen.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.080
Michael's my attorney and
you'll have to ask Michael.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.960
- [Narrator] Days later, FBI
agents raided Cohen's home,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:13.980
which Trump called...

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.300
- A disgraceful situation.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.380
It's a total witch hunt.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.060
I've been saying it for a long time.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.740
- [Narrator] Federal
prosecutors charged Cohen

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.980
with campaign finance violations
and other federal crimes.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.470
He pleaded guilty to all of the charges,

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.000
telling a federal judge at the time

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.540
that Trump had directed him
to buy Daniels' silence.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.200
- I am providing the committee
today with several documents,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.860
and these include a copy of the check

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.130
Mr. Trump wrote from his
personal bank account

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:45.150
after he became President to reimburse me

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.460
for the hush money payments I made

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.210
to cover up his affair
with an adult film star

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.850
and to prevent damage to his campaign.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.280
- [Narrator] Despite Cohen
implicating Trump in the crime

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.710
federal prosecutors dropped the case,

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.800
but that still left the
possibility of state charges

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.740
as the Trump organization
is based in New York.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.010
Cyrus Vance, the Manhattan
District Attorney, stepped in.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.370
Ultimately, the DA's office
decided not to bring charges.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.070
When Vance retired, the
new DA, Alvin Bragg,

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.870
initially decided not to pursue

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.580
the hush money investigation.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.980
- There is a felony of falsifying
business records charge

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.030
but that requires the records
to have been falsified

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.880
to conceal another crime
or to commit another crime.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.040
And, you know, the
obvious other crime here

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.210
is the campaign finance crime,

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.920
the actual payoff of Stormy Daniels

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.570
to protect Donald Trump's campaign.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.360
But there has never
been a case or a judge,

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.700
a state judge has never blessed the use

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.940
of felony falsifying business records

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.190
premised on a federal charge.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.360
In other words, these
are state prosecutors,

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.800
they're bringing a state charge

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.050
and in order to elevate it to a felony

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.930
they have to say that the
crime that was concealed

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.420
by falsifying these business
records was a federal crime.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.680
So that's like a weird thing.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.720
And they decided it was gonna be too risky

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.980
to bring a case that was gonna rely

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.420
on an untested legal theory.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.800
- [Narrator] But then, in January,

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.540
Bragg impaneled a new grand jury

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.070
to investigate the payments.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.560
He hasn't said publicly
why he changed course.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.360
- Everyone's surprised, frankly,

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.420
because our reporting and others had shown

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.310
that the office had looked
at this so many times,

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.470
had looked at it through
kind of different lenses

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.390
and decided each time not to bring it.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.280
The feds had passed up on
the chance to bring it.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.480
So, now, here we are in
2023 and what's changed?

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.430
I mean we don't, we don't really know yet.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.020
- [Narrator] One thing that hasn't changed

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.400
is Cohen's involvement.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.930
Trump's former lawyer testified

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.640
before the grand jury last week

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.805
and could be called to
speak with them again.

00:04:34.805 --> 00:04:36.625
- This is all about accountability.

00:04:36.625 --> 00:04:40.320
He needs to be held accountable
for his dirty deeds.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.200
- [Narrator] Trump has denied
the affair and any wrongdoing,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.020
calling the investigation
politically motivated.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.120
The Manhattan DA's office did not respond

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.560
to request for comment.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.800
If Bragg brings charges
against the former president

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.830
it could shine more light
on what happened in 2016.

00:04:56.745 --> 00:04:58.590
- An indictment's just
an allegation, right?

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.450
There are still, you know,
questions that I have

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.790
even after having worked
on this for so long.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.700
If the charges are focused on
falsifying business records,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.580
you know, like what did Trump
know about repaying Cohen?

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.260
There's a lot of sort
of gaps in our knowledge

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.820
about how this all went down.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.470
And then, you know, I'm
really curious to see

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.750
if the DA has like learned some new facts.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:19.380
Charges, if they come, I think
would would sort of begin

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.957
like just one more chapter.

00:05:20.957 --> 00:05:23.374
(Joe laughs)

